# The single-page fallback, and why it is not optional.
#
# The app routes by service slug (#335): the first path segment names the
# active service, so `/plus-tutoring?cell=<id>` is a real address that
# `serviceRoute.ts` reads on load and `urlViewState.ts` reads alongside it.
# Netlify serves the build directory as static files, and there is no
# `plus-tutoring/index.html` in it — so without this rule every such address
# is a 404 on a fresh load. Only the bare `/` worked, and only because it is
# the one file that does exist.
#
# That was live: `/` answered 200 and `/plus-tutoring` answered 404, while the
# app itself rewrote the URL to `/plus-tutoring` the moment it booted. A reader
# who bookmarked what the address bar showed them, or reloaded the page they
# were on, got Netlify's 404 for a route the app owns.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser keeps the address it asked for, so the app
# still reads the slug and the query params out of it. A redirect would throw
# both away.
#
# Everything sits under `/blueprint/`, the BASE_PATH in `netlify.toml`: the
# build writes its files there, and the board is shown at
# plus-uno.netlify.app/blueprint through a proxy that forwards the path
# unchanged. The same rules therefore answer both ways in.

# Nothing is served at this site's own root any more, so a bare `/` would be a
# 404. It is sent to the board instead. It matches `/` alone, so it shadows
# nothing below, and it is a 302 rather than a 301 so a browser does not keep
# it forever if the root is ever given something of its own.
/    /blueprint/    302

# A missing hashed asset is a 404, not the app shell.
#
# Netlify takes the first rule that matches, so this one has to sit above the
# fallback: a stale tab asking for a chunk from a previous deploy would
# otherwise fall through and be handed `index.html` with a 200 and a
# `text/html` type, which the browser reports as a failed dynamic import
# rather than as the missing file it is. `:splat` keeps the real path so a
# chunk that IS there is still served; only the ones that are not answer 404.
# The catch-all below must stay last.
/blueprint/assets/*    /blueprint/assets/:splat    404

/blueprint/*    /blueprint/index.html   200
